  "notes": "Searched all ten themes in Hardin's two essays, Heilbroner's essay, Lovelock's interview, Hulme's review and four scholarly papers; the thinkers write on population, coercion, growth and the failure of democracy and are silent on most else, so most answers are null. William Ophuls's books are borrow-only on archive.org and could not be opened, and Shearman and Smith's book was only read through Hulme. Hardin's lifeboat positions (aid, immigration) were not answered because no other strand source shares them. Heilbroner forecasts rather than recommends authoritarianism."
